64dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37f8b53b48dd952fbd12c939446574298771be85845af31bcd6f1b2d3468d28d"} {"question" "q-117338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{6}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\n- $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\n- $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37f8b53b48dd952fbd12c939446574298771be85845af31bcd6f1b2d3468d28d"} {"question" "q-117366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\n- $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n- $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3})$\n- $(0,0)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117371" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{7\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{7\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(0,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,0)$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038821/state.json" "file_sha256" "86e06db327268664dbc6a1935ef05bd35a624b1e196fe83743448925bc2ecd37"} {"question" "q-117371" "field" nil "attribute